   "summary": "Welcome to Module 4 of IL-05 — Cloud DevSecOps Platform SRE. I'm your instructor, and this module is HashiCorp Terraform through the Associate (003) exam. We'll write HCL the way the exam thinks — resources, providers, data sources, variables, outputs, locals — then run the core workflow until it's reflex: init, validate, plan, apply, destroy. State is the crown jewels, so we give it the full treatment: remote backends, locking, import, and refactoring moves. Then module composition, workspaces, and the Associate exam's domain map with exam-day logistics. The exam loves 'what happens when' — we reason every answer from the state model, not from memorization.",
