  {
   "cards": [
    {
     "front": "Front Door vs Application Gateway?",
     "back": "Front Door: global edge, instant failover. App Gateway: regional L7 + WAF."
    },
    {
     "front": "Traffic Manager routing basis?",
     "back": "DNS — failover takes TTL time. Not instant like Front Door."
    },
    {
     "front": "Private Link vs service endpoint?",
     "back": "Private Link: PaaS gets VNet-private IP (stronger). Service endpoint: VNet identity, PaaS still public."
    },
    {
     "front": "ExpressRoute value?",
     "back": "Private, consistent-latency circuit — not internet VPN variability."
    },
    {
     "front": "Bastion replaces?",
     "back": "Internet-facing jumpboxes — browser RDP/SSH, no public IPs to patch."
    },
    {
     "front": "VNet address overlap with on-prem?",
     "back": "Fatal for peering/VPN — plan non-overlapping CIDRs up front, forever."
    },
    {
     "front": "Front Door vs Traffic Manager failover?",
     "back": "Front Door: instant at the edge. Traffic Manager: DNS-level, takes TTL time."
    },
    {
     "front": "Gateway transit in peering?",
     "back": "Spokes use the hub VPN/ExpressRoute gateway — enable use-remote-gateways on the spoke side."
    },
    {
     "front": "FQDN filtering: which control?",
     "back": "Azure Firewall — NSGs filter IPs/ports, not domain names."
    },
    {
     "front": "AZ-700 core skill?",
     "back": "Selection by constraint — which service the scenario demands, not syntax."
    },
    {
     "front": "Global web app, instant regional failover, WAF?",
     "back": "**Front Door** — Front Door: global edge + instant failover + WAF — the global L7 answer. — see 'Concepts' in this module's notes."
    },
    {
     "front": "SQL PaaS must be VNet-private?",
     "back": "**Private Endpoint (Private Link)** — Private Endpoint puts SQL on a VNet-private IP — off the public internet. — see 'Concepts' in this module's notes."
    }
   ],
