  {
   "cards": [
    {
     "front": "GitOps in one line?",
     "back": "Desired state declared in git; agents converge the cluster — git is truth, cluster is cache."
    },
    {
     "front": "rate() over what metric type?",
     "back": "Counters — never gauges. The PromQL trap."
    },
    {
     "front": "eBPF's trick?",
     "back": "Safe kernel programs — Cilium does networking/observability without kube-proxy iptables."
    },
    {
     "front": "Cilium vs Calico policy depth?",
     "back": "Cilium: L3-L7 (HTTP-aware). Calico: L3/L4. eBPF vs iptables dataplane."
    },
    {
     "front": "Argo Rollouts provide?",
     "back": "Progressive delivery (canary/blue-green) as Kubernetes CRDs."
    },
    {
     "front": "Associate exam format?",
     "back": "Proctored multiple-choice — vocabulary + concepts; performance depth is the CKA/CKAD/CKS tier."
    },
    {
     "front": "Prometheus metric types?",
     "back": "Counter, gauge, histogram, summary. rate() goes over counters — never gauges."
    },
    {
     "front": "Argo CD vs kubectl apply?",
     "back": "Argo CD: continuous reconciliation from git with drift detection. kubectl apply: one-shot imperative."
    },
    {
     "front": "Sync waves order?",
     "back": "CRDs and namespaces first, then the apps that need them — complex deploys need ordering."
    },
    {
     "front": "Why KCNA before CKA?",
     "back": "Vocabulary before performance: the architecture and principles pay back immediately under the 2-hour clock."
    },
    {
     "front": "Cluster state drifted from git. GitOps response?",
     "back": "**Argo CD detects drift; sync (auto or manual) reconverges** — Drift detection + sync — the cluster converges back to git's declared state. — see 'Concepts' in this module's notes."
    },
    {
     "front": "PromQL: request rate from a counter?",
